  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0ee850c578174c94a8ac88fe209aae22, type: 3}
  m_Name: InteractDialogue
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ScriptableObjectDialogu
  dialogueLines:
  - _characterIcon: {fileID: -3607883123437360786, guid: 3ac0368c78cff2048958d9e1d88a407b, type: 3}
    line: I love how collected items immediately fill my inventory. SO handy.
  - _characterIcon: {fileID: -3607883123437360786, guid: 3ac0368c78cff2048958d9e1d88a407b, type: 3}
    line: Time to solve the levels puzzle. Each paper has a code on it that I need
      to input into the lock to progress.
  - _characterIcon: {fileID: -3607883123437360786, guid: 3ac0368c78cff2048958d9e1d88a407b, type: 3}
    line: As designer of the game I know the answer, of course, but best to test
      the lock by inputting both codes.
  - _characterIcon: {fileID: -3607883123437360786, guid: 3ac0368c78cff2048958d9e1d88a407b, type: 3}
    line: I just need to click the item to select it then press E to enter the code.
